                  Google's Core Web Vitals prioritize fast-loading websites, and Time to First Byte (TTFB) measures how quickly your server responds to a browser request. A slow TTFB delays Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) and First Input Delay (FID). Hosting WordPress on enterprise AMD EPYC CPUs with PCIe 4.0 NVMe SSDs and LiteSpeed caching keeps TTFB under 200ms, directly improving crawl efficiency and organic search rank.
